.TH CTPOOL_DESTROY 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ctpool_destroy \- destroy a thread pool and invalidate the handle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ctpool_destroy(pool);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls __ctpool_destroy() to wait for every in-flight resolved use of
the handle to finish, drain or cancel all pending tasks, join all
worker threads, and free all associated resources. The pool handle
is then set to CTPOOL_INVALID.

If neither ctpool_shutdown_drain() nor ctpool_shutdown_immediate() was
called beforehand, a drain shutdown is performed implicitly so that all
queued tasks complete before the pool is freed.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool  Thread pool variable to destroy (set to CTPOOL_INVALID after
      destruction).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call when pool is CTPOOL_INVALID (no-op). Calling this on a
stale handle (one already destroyed, sequentially by an earlier
call or concurrently by another thread) is a FATAL ERROR
(abort()/SIGABRT), not a silent double-free; see __ctpool_destroy(3)
for further detail.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_construct (3),
.BR __ctpool_destroy (3),
.BR ctpool_shutdown_drain (3),
.BR ctpool_shutdown_immediate (3)
